# Who may read and write what.
#
# Everything ChatNyto does lives under chatnyto/, so authenticated users get
# that subtree and nothing else. The payloads are end-to-end encrypted, so a
# shared subtree does not mean shared readable messages — but keeping the
# rest of the broker closed avoids it being used as a general-purpose relay.

# Authenticated users: full access to the app's tree.
pattern readwrite chatnyto/#

# A dedicated monitoring account, if you create one, may only read $SYS.
user monitor
topic read $SYS/#
